{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\n// Defined in habeas_sdk::procedure.\npub struct AgentInput<'i, D: Graph> {\n    pub node: &'i D::NodeId,\n    pub contents: &'i D::NodeContent,\n}\n\npub trait AgentInputRenderer<D: Graph>: Send + Sync {\n    /// Present these supplied contents without fetching replacement contents.\n    fn render(&self, input: &AgentInput<'_, D>) -> Result<String, D::Error>;\n}\n```\n\nThe application supplies the renderer through `Validator::with_agent`.\nRendering errors return `ValidationError::Graph`. Neither `Graph::NodeContent`\nnor `Graph::NodeId` needs serialization or display bounds.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\nObligations, with the tests that cover each:\n\n- **Render the supplied contents without fetching replacements.**\n  - `validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` checks that the contents handed to the agent are the rendered, supplied contents, in order and with repeats. It also asserts the graph's read log is exactly `[1,3,2,3,1]`, one read per insertion, so rendering fetched nothing extra.\n  - `agent.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` checks that the rendered text (\"source\") appears in the chat history.\n  - `agent.rs#fn[validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` uses a `DistinctPages` renderer whose output depends on `input.node` and `input.contents`. Two concurrent conversations each get their own rendering, and the recorded dependencies are correct.\n  - `AgentInput` carries only `node` and `contents`, so a renderer cannot fetch anything itself.\n- **The application supplies the renderer through `Validator::with_agent`.** `agent.rs#fn[validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` builds `Validator::new(&graph).with_agent(&agent, &agent.renderer)` and verifies through it. `validation.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` checks that a validator without an agent returns `NoAgentConfigured` and stores nothing. Once `with_agent(&agent, &Renderer)` is added, the rendered contents work and the dependencies are recorded.\n- **Rendering errors return `ValidationError::Graph`.** `validation.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` uses `FailingRenderer`, which returns `Err(\"render\")`. It asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"render\"))`, that no dependencies are recorded, and that the agent request count is unchanged, so the agent was not invoked.\n- **`NodeContent` and `NodeId` need no serialization or display bounds.** The `Node` type in `agent.rs` deliberately derives only `Clone`, `Eq` and `PartialEq`, with no Serde, Hash or Display. The tests that use it compile and run through rendering and dependency recording, which shows the trait and context work without those bounds.\n\nThe `agent.rs` edge-only test uses a renderer that panics if called. That test shows that rendering happens only for explicitly requested contents, which is consistent with the requirement.\n\nNo test gap was found, and there are no acknowledgments.",
  "references": "ce598c21f57eca7ac1b06bdbfe846984a4b6be33ce0b6dff069ac85731ec6453",
